 to spend 20 + 30 + 120 + 10 = 180 minutes.\nShe wants to serve the cake at 5:00 pm.\nSo she has to start making the cake at 5:00 pm - 180 minutes = 2:00 pm.\nThe answer is 2:00 pm.\n\nAnswer_21:\nLisa sold 3.5 boxes of chocolate bars.\nPeter sold 4.5 boxes of chocolate bars.\nThey sold 64 chocolate bars together.\nSo each box has 64 / (3.5 + 4.5) = 64 / 8 = 8 chocolate bars.\nThe answer is 8.\n\nAnswer_22:\nThe dance studio has 10 students.\nIt rents the studio 3 days a week.\nSo it rents the studio 3 * 4 = 12 days a month.\nIt costs $25 per session to rent the studio.\nSo it costs 25 * 12 = $300 to rent the studio.\nIt costs $1.50 per student per session.\nSo it costs 1.5 * 10 * 12 = $180 to pay the students.\nSo the expected earnings of the dance studio in a month is 300 + 180 = $480.\nThe answer is 480.\n\nAnswer_23:\nPeter has 4 boxes with the same number of chocolate bars in each.\nMartha has 7 boxes with the same number of chocolate bars in each.\nPeter has a total of 64 chocolate bars.\nMartha has a total of 56 chocolate bars.\nSo Peter has 64 / 4 = 16 chocolate bars in each box.\nMartha has 56 / 7 = 8 chocolate bars in each box.\nSo Peter has 16 - 8 = 8 more chocolate bars in each box than Martha.\nThe answer is 8.\n\nAnswer_24:\nThe number of female porcupines is 3/5 of the total population.\nSo there are 3/5 * 50 = 30 female porcupines.\nEach female porcupine gives birth to 4 babies every month.\nSo there are 30 * 4 = 120 new porcupines every month.\nThere are 12 months in a year.\nSo there are 120 * 12 = 1440 new porcupines in a year.\nThe answer is 1440.\n\nAnswer_25:\nThe pool is 14 feet wide, 25 feet long, and 4 feet deep.\nSo the volume of the pool is 14 * 25 * 4 = 1400 cubic feet.\nThe pool company instructed them to multiply the volume by 5.9.\nSo they need 1400 * 5.9 = 8280 gallons of water.\nThe cost for the pool company to come and fill the pool is $0.10 per gallon.\nSo it will cost 8280 * 0.10 = $828 to fill the pool.\nThe answer is 828.\n\nAnswer_26:\nThere are 9 red sticks.\nThere are 5 more blue sticks than red.\nSo there are 9 + 5 = 14 blue sticks.\nThere are 3 less yellow sticks than blue.\nSo there are 14 - 3 = 11 yellow sticks.\nSo they have 9 + 14 + 11 = 34 sticks.\nThe answer is 34.\n\nAnswer_27:\nMatteo traveled at 55 miles per hour for 4 hours.\nSo he traveled 55 * 4 = 220 miles.\nShandy traveled at 45 miles per hour for 10 hours.\nSo he traveled 45 * 10 = 450 miles.\nShandy traveled 450 - 220 = 230 miles farther than Matteo.\nThe answer is 230.\n\nAnswer_28:\nHalf of the students are over 16 years old.\nSo there are 3000 / 2 = 1500 students over 16 years old.\nOne-fourth of the students over 16 years old are male.\nSo there are 1500 / 4 = 375 male students over 16 years old.\nThe remaining half of the students are under 16 years old.\nSo there are 3000 / 2 = 1500 students under 16 years old.\nOne-half of the students under 16 are male.\nSo there are 1500 / 2 = 750 male students under 16 years old.\nThere are 375 + 750 = 1125 male students in total.\nThere are 3000 - 1125 = 1875 female students in total.\nThe answer is 1875.\n\nAnswer_29:\nBethany can run 10 laps.\nTrey can run 4 more laps than Bethany.\nSo Trey can run 10 + 4 = 14 laps.\nShaelyn can run half as many laps as Trey.\nSo Shaelyn can run 14 / 2 = 7 laps.\nQuinn can run 2 fewer laps than Shaelyn.\nSo Quinn can run 7 - 2 = 5 laps.\nBethany can run 10 laps.\nQuinn can run 5 laps.\nSo Bethany can run 10 - 5 = 5 more laps than Quinn.\nThe answer is 5.\n\nAnswer_30:\nWanda filled 1/4 of the tank's capacity with water on the first day.\nSo she filled 1/4 * 18000 = 4500 gallons of water.\nMs. B pumped 3/4 as much water as Wanda pumped into the tank that day.\nSo Ms. B pumped 3/4 * 4500 = 3375 gallons of water.\nOn the second day, Wanda pumped 2/3 of the amount of water she pumped on the previous day.\nSo Wanda pumped 2/3 * 4500 = 3000 gallons of water.\nMs. B pumped 1/3 of the number of gallons she pumped on the first day.\nSo Ms. B pumped 1/3 * 3375 = 1125 gallons of water.\nWanda filled 4500 gallons of water on the first day.\nWanda filled 3000 gallons of water on the second day.\nSo Wanda filled 4500 + 3000 = 7500 gallons of water in total.\nMs. B filled 3375 gallons of water on the first day.\nMs. B filled 1125 gallons of water on the second day.\nSo Ms. B filled 3375 + 1125 = 4500 gallons of water in total.\nWanda and Ms. B filled 7500 + 4500 = 12000 gallons of water in total.\nThe tank has a capacity of 18000 gallons.\nSo there are 18000 - 12000 = 6000 gallons of water remaining for the tank to be full.\nThe answer is 6000.\n\nAnswer_31:\nMaria's power bank loses 9% of its capacity each hour.\nSo after 5 hours, it loses 9% * 5 = 45% of its capacity.\nAfter 5 hours, it has 100 - 45 = 55% of its capacity left.\nThen it loses 7% of its capacity each hour for 3 hours.\nSo it loses 7% * 3 = 21% of its capacity.\nAfter 3 hours, it has 55 - 21 = 34% of its capacity left.\nSo it has 34% of its capacity left after 8 hours.\nThe charge remaining is 28%.\nSo the charge when Maria went out to the park is 28 / 34 = 82.35% of its capacity.\nThe answer is 82.35%.\n\nAnswer_32:\nJanet makes $10 an hour from wages.\nShe makes $15 an hour from tips.\nSo she makes 10 + 15 = 25 dollars an hour.\nShe wants to save up 20% of the cost of a $10000 car.\nSo she wants to save 0.2 * 10000 = 2000 dollars.\nShe works 40 hours a week.\nSo she makes 25 * 40 = 1000 dollars a week.\nShe wants to save 2000 dollars.\nSo she needs to work 2000 / 1000 = 2 weeks.\nThe answer is 2.\n\nAnswer_33:\nJamaar has $10.\nPeaches cost $0.5 each.\nPears cost $0.5 each.\nApples cost $0.75 each.\nKiwis cost $1 each.\nPlums cost $0.25 each.\nHe has already purchased 3 peaches, 4 pears, 2 kiwis, and 5 apples.\nSo he has spent 3 * 0.5 + 4 * 0.5 + 2 * 1 + 5 * 0.75 = 1.5 + 2 + 2 + 3.75 = 8.25 dollars.\nHe has $10 left.\nSo he can spend 10 - 8.25 = 1.75 dollars.\nPlums cost $0.25 each.\nSo he can buy 1.75 / 0.25 = 7 plums.\nThe answer is 7.\n\nAnswer_34:\nAnne kept 2 packs of sweets.\nSo she gave 15 - 2 = 13 packs to her friends.\nShe gave the sweets equally to her 10 friends.\nSo each friend got 13 / 10 = 1.3 packs of sweets.\nThe answer is 1.3.\n\nAnswer_35:\nThe price of carrots increases by 5% every year.\nSo after one year, the price is 120 * 1.05 = 126 dollars.\nAfter two years, the price is 126 * 1.05 = 132.3 dollars.\nAfter three years, the price is 132.3 * 1.05 = 138.915 dollars.\nRounded to the nearest integer, the price is 139 dollars.\nThe answer is 139.\n\nAnswer_36:\nOlivia uploaded 72 pictures to Facebook.\nShe put the same number of pictures into 8 albums.\nSo she put 72 / 8 = 9 pictures into each album.\n3 of the albums were selfies only.\nSo she had 3 * 9 = 27 selfies.\n2 of the albums were portraits.\nSo she had 2 * 9 = 18 portraits.\nThe answer is 18.\n\nAnswer_37:\nJames reads 3 pages in 10 minutes.\nSo he reads 1 page in 10 / 3 = 3.33 minutes.\nHe reads 18 pages.\nSo he reads 18 * 3.33 = 60 minutes.\nThe answer is 60.\n\nAnswer_38:\n24 guests elected an early checkout.\n15 guests elected a late checkout.\nSo 24 + 15 = 39 guests left.\nIn the afternoon, twice as many people checked in as those who opted for a late checkout.\nSo 2 * 15 = 30 people checked in.\n7 more people checked in after dinner.\nSo 30 + 7 = 37 people checked in.\nThere were 100 guests originally.\nSo there are 100 - 39 = 61 guests left.\nThen 37 people checked in.\nSo there are 61 + 37 = 98 guests now.\nThe answer is 98.",
